                <pb facs="0534" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1266.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-04-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                    1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Vice President Corral has been granted leave of absence for eight months by
                    Congress, and he will depart for Europe within a few days. As he did not resign
                    the situation is further complicated. [Revolutionist attacks reported.] The
                    governors of most of the Mexican States and their subordinates are being
                    replaced.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
